IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc18-soira-notice`
IMPORT `ccc18-soira-foreign`

-- ccc18-tests-soira-foreign.l4 -- tests for ccc18-soira-foreign.l4. Expected values are written from the text of the Criminal Code
-- (R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, lines 10275-10956 of the plain-text rendering), beside each assertion, and not copied from the module's own output.

#ASSERT `s 490.02901 the person shall comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02901 the person shall comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless a court makes an exemption order"
#ASSERT `s 490.02901 the person shall comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not served
-- no time is stated beyond the period of section 490.02904; the trace has no WITHIN; the person complies: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02901 the duty of the offender to comply` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the offender` DOES `s 490.02901 comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act for the applicable period specified in section 490.02904` AT 1

-- 490.02902(1): "only if" the person arrived on or after 15 April 2011, was convicted (or found NCR) of an offence outside Canada other than a service offence, equivalent in the opinion of the Attorney General or minister.
#ASSERT `s 490.02902(1) the Attorney General or minister of justice may serve the person with a notice in Form 54` (Date 15 4 2011) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- arrived on the day
#ASSERT `s 490.02902(1) the Attorney General or minister of justice may serve the person with a notice in Form 54` (Date 14 4 2011) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a day before
#ASSERT `s 490.02902(1) the Attorney General or minister of justice may serve the person with a notice in Form 54` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not convicted outside Canada
#ASSERT `s 490.02902(1) the Attorney General or minister of justice may serve the person with a notice in Form 54` (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a service offence
#ASSERT `s 490.02902(1) the Attorney General or minister of justice may serve the person with a notice in Form 54` (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not equivalent in the opinion of the Attorney General or minister

#ASSERT `s 490.02902(2) a notice shall not be served on the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02902(2) a notice shall not be served on the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.02902 the notice in Form 54 may be served, subject to subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490.02902 the notice in Form 54 may be served, subject to subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02902 the notice in Form 54 may be served, subject to subsection (2)` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 490.02903(1) the manner of service is the one the subsection requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02903(1) the manner of service is the one the subsection requires` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 490.02903(2) the affidavit is evidence of the service and the notice` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02903(2) the affidavit is evidence of the service and the notice` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490.02903(2) the affidavit is evidence of the service and the notice` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490.02903(2) the affidavit is evidence of the service and the notice` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b): this section has no "or mailed to"
#ASSERT `s 490.02903(2) the affidavit is evidence of the service and the notice` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 490.02903(3) the person who served the notice must send a copy of the affidavit and the notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02903(3) the person who served the notice must send a copy of the affidavit and the notice` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02903(3) the duty of the person who served the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 490.02903(3) the person who served the notice` DOES `s 490.02903(3) send a copy of the affidavit and the notice to the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the person was served` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.02904(1) the day on which the obligation under section 490.02901 begins` (Date 3 5 2018) EQUALS Date 3 5 2018

#ASSERT `s 490.02904(2) the day on which the obligation ends` (JUST (Date 3 5 2019)) EQUALS JUST (Date 3 5 2019)
#ASSERT `s 490.02904(2) the day on which the obligation ends` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- 490.02904(3): the maximum term "provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence"; sentenced on 1 June 2012.
#ASSERT `s 490.02904(3) the obligation, if subsection (2) does not apply, ends or applies for life` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`) (Date 1 6 2012) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2022))
#ASSERT `s 490.02904(3) the obligation, if subsection (2) does not apply, ends or applies for life` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) (Date 1 6 2012) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2022))
#ASSERT `s 490.02904(3) the obligation, if subsection (2) does not apply, ends or applies for life` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) (Date 1 6 2012) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2032))
#ASSERT `s 490.02904(3) the obligation, if subsection (2) does not apply, ends or applies for life` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`) (Date 1 6 2012) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2032))
#ASSERT `s 490.02904(3) the obligation, if subsection (2) does not apply, ends or applies for life` `imprisonment for life` (Date 1 6 2012) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 490.022(3) applies for life`
#ASSERT `s 490.02904(3) the obligation, if subsection (2) does not apply, ends or applies for life` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) (Date 1 6 2012) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 490.022(3) applies for life`   -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 490.02904(3) the obligation, if subsection (2) does not apply, ends or applies for life` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) (Date 1 6 2012) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2022))   -- (d) needs both
#ASSERT `s 490.02904(3) the obligation, if subsection (2) does not apply, ends or applies for life` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE)) (Date 1 6 2012) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 490.02905(1): served on 1 March 2019; the year runs to 1 March 2020.
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 3 2019) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 3 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- last day
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 2 3 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a day late
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 28 2 2019) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before service
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 6 2019) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not to a court of criminal jurisdiction
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` FALSE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 6 2019) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not served with a Form 54 notice

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2) the court shall make an exemption order` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 1 of 4 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2) the court shall make an exemption order` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 2 of 4 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2) the court shall make an exemption order` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 3 of 4 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2) the court shall make an exemption order` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 4 of 4 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2) the court shall make an exemption order` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not satisfied of any ground
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2) the court shall make an exemption order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every ground
-- the text gives no time for the order, so the trace has no WITHIN; the court makes the order: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02905(2) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.02905(2) make an exemption order` AT 1

-- s 490.02905(2.1): each factor in the list is one the court shall consider, when it is determining the order; (g) adds any matter the court considers relevant.

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02905(2.1)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02905(2.1)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02905(2.1)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02905(2.1)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02905(2.1)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02905(2.1)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02905(2.1)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02905(2.1) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the court considers it relevant: paragraph (g)

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02905(2.1) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not named, and the court does not consider it relevant

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2.1) the court shall consider the factor` FALSE `s 490.02905(2.1)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not determining the order

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2.2) the court shall order that the notice be corrected` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(2.2) the court shall order that the notice be corrected` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02905(2.2) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.02905(2.2) order that the notice be corrected` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(3) the court shall give reasons for its decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(3) the court shall give reasons for its decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02905(3) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.02905(3) give reasons for its decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(4) the court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(4) the court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02905(4) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.02905(4) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of the copy of the notice` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.02905(5) the court shall cause the notification to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02905(5) the court shall cause the notification to be given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02905(5) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.02905(5) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.029051(1) the person may apply for a variation order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 3 2020) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029051(1) the person may apply for a variation order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 2 3 2020) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a day late
#ASSERT `s 490.029051(1) the person may apply for a variation order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 6 2019) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (a) not met
#ASSERT `s 490.029051(1) the person may apply for a variation order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 6 2019) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (b) not met
#ASSERT `s 490.029051(1) the person may apply for a variation order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 6 2019) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not to a court of criminal jurisdiction
#ASSERT `s 490.029051(1) the person may apply for a variation order` FALSE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 6 2019) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not served

#ASSERT `s 490.029051(2) the court shall make the variation order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 1 of 1 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.029051(2) the court shall make the variation order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not satisfied of any ground
-- the text gives no time for the order, so the trace has no WITHIN; the court makes the order: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.029051(2) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.029051(2) make the variation order` AT 1

-- 490.029051(3): paragraphs 490.02904(3)(a) and (b) applied to the offence whose equivalent has the longest maximum term; sentenced 1 June 2012.
#ASSERT `s 490.029051(3) the duration of the obligation set out in the variation order` TRUE (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) (Date 1 6 2012) EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2022))
#ASSERT `s 490.029051(3) the duration of the obligation set out in the variation order` TRUE (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`) (Date 1 6 2012) EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2032))
#ASSERT `s 490.029051(3) the duration of the obligation set out in the variation order` TRUE `imprisonment for life` (Date 1 6 2012) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.029051(3) the duration of the obligation set out in the variation order` FALSE (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) (Date 1 6 2012) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no variation order made
#TRACE `s 490.029051(3) the duty of the court to set out the duration` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.029051(3) set out the duration of the obligation in the variation order` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.029051(4) the court shall give reasons for its decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029051(4) the court shall give reasons for its decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.029051(4) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.029051(4) give reasons for its decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.029051(5) the court shall cause the notification to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029051(5) the court shall cause the notification to be given` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.029051(5) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.029051(5) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of a variation order made under this section` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.02906(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.02906(1) the Attorney General` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02906(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.02906(1) the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02906(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.02906(1) another person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another person
#ASSERT `s 490.02906(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.02906(1) the Attorney General` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a different decision
#ASSERT `s 490.02906(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.02906(1) the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a ground raising no question of law or mixed law and fact

#ASSERT `s 490.02906(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.02906(1) dismiss the appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02906(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.02906(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02906(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.02906(1) quash the exemption order or variation order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02906(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.02906(1) amend the exemption order or variation order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02906(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.02906(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.02905(2) or (2.2) or 490.029051(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02906(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.02906(1) another thing` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.02906(2) the appeal court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02906(2) the appeal court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02906(2) the duty of a court of appeal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.02906(2) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of the copy of the notice` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.02907(1) the appeal court shall cause the notification and the information to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02907(1) the appeal court shall cause the notification and the information to be given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 490.02907(1) the duty of the appeal court to cause the Commissioner and the Attorney General to be notified` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.02907(1) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision` AT 1
#TRACE `s 490.02907(1) the duty of the appeal court to cause the person to be informed of the sections` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.02907(1) cause the person who applied for the order to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.02907(2) the appeal court shall cause the notification to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02907(2) the appeal court shall cause the notification to be given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02907(2) the duty of a court of appeal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.02907(2) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.02908(1) the person may apply for a termination order` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02908(1) the person may apply for a termination order` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless": another obligation or order that began later
#ASSERT `s 490.02908(1) the person may apply for a termination order` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.02908(1) the person may apply for a termination order` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not to a court of criminal jurisdiction
