#TRACE `s 490.02909(3) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.02909(3) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, to be notified of the decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.0291(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.0291(1) the Attorney General` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.0291(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.0291(1) the person who applied for a termination order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.0291(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.0291(1) another person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another person
#ASSERT `s 490.0291(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.0291(1) the Attorney General` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a different decision
#ASSERT `s 490.0291(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.0291(1) the person who applied for a termination order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a ground raising no question of law or mixed law and fact

#ASSERT `s 490.0291(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.0291(1) dismiss the appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.0291(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.0291(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.0291(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.0291(1) quash the termination order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.0291(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.0291(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.02909(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.0291(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.0291(1) another thing` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.0291(2) the appeal court shall cause the notification to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.0291(2) the appeal court shall cause the notification to be given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.0291(2) the duty of a court of appeal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.0291(2) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision` AT 1

-- 490.02911(1): the duty arises for a person convicted or found NCR outside Canada where the offence is equivalent to one in para (a) of "primary offence".
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the person must advise a police service` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the person must advise a police service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "if the offence is equivalent"
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the person must advise a police service` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not convicted outside Canada
-- within seven days after the day of arrival (arrived 1 March 2019: seven days after is 8 March 2019; the arrival day itself is in time: fork F6)
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the person advised a police service within seven days after the day on which they arrived in Canada` (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 8 3 2019) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- last day
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the person advised a police service within seven days after the day on which they arrived in Canada` (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 9 3 2019) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day late
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the person advised a police service within seven days after the day on which they arrived in Canada` (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 3 2019) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- on arrival
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the person advised a police service within seven days after the day on which they arrived in Canada` (Date 28 2 2019) (Date 7 3 2019) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- across a month end: 28 February plus seven days is 7 March
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the person advised a police service within seven days after the day on which they arrived in Canada` (Date 28 2 2019) (Date 8 3 2019) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the person advised a police service within seven days after the day on which they arrived in Canada` (Date 5 3 2019) (Date 4 3 2019) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before arrival
-- the advice: (a) five particulars, (b)(i) to (iv) to the best of their knowledge, and (v) when the sentence day differs.
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the advice covers what the subsection lists` (`s 490.02911(1) the advice` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- same day: (v) needs nothing
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the advice covers what the subsection lists` (`s 490.02911(1) the advice` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- different day, given
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the advice covers what the subsection lists` (`s 490.02911(1) the advice` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- different day, not given
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the advice covers what the subsection lists` (`s 490.02911(1) the advice` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no name
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the advice covers what the subsection lists` (`s 490.02911(1) the advice` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no telephone number
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1) the advice covers what the subsection lists` (`s 490.02911(1) the advice` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no country
-- the rule, in days from arrival: advise on day 7 (inside "within seven days"): expected FULFILLED; nothing by day 8: expected BREACH
#TRACE `s 490.02911(1) the duty of the offender to advise a police service within seven days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the offender` DOES `s 490.02911(1) advise a police service of the fact and of the particulars in paragraphs (a) and (b)` AT 7
#TRACE `s 490.02911(1) the duty of the offender to advise a police service within seven days` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 8

#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1.1) the person is required to advise the police service again` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(1.1) the person is required to advise the police service again` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 490.02911(2) the person must advise a police service of a change in address` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(2) the person must advise a police service of a change in address` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "if they are in Canada"
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(2) the person advised a police service of the change in address within seven days after the day on which the change was made` (Date 10 5 2019) (Date 17 5 2019) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(2) the person advised a police service of the change in address within seven days after the day on which the change was made` (Date 10 5 2019) (Date 18 5 2019) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(2) the person advised a police service of the change in address within seven days after the day on which the change was made` (Date 10 5 2019) (Date 9 5 2019) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 490.02911(2) the duty of the offender to advise a police service of a change in address within seven days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the offender` DOES `s 490.02911(2) advise a police service of a change in address` AT 7
#TRACE `s 490.02911(2) the duty of the offender to advise a police service of a change in address within seven days` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 8

#ASSERT `s 490.02911(3) the police service shall cause the Attorney General or minister of justice to be provided with the information` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(3) the police service shall cause the Attorney General or minister of justice to be provided with the information` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02911(3) the duty of a police service` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 490.02911(3) a police service` DOES `s 490.02911(3) cause the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which it is located to be provided with the information` AT 1

-- 490.02911(4): ends when served under 490.02902 or, if it is earlier, one year after the day they advise under (1).
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(4) the day on which the obligation under subsection (2) ends` (JUST (Date 1 9 2019)) (JUST (Date 1 3 2019)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2019)   -- served before the year ends
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(4) the day on which the obligation under subsection (2) ends` (JUST (Date 1 9 2020)) (JUST (Date 1 3 2019)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2020)   -- the year ends first
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(4) the day on which the obligation under subsection (2) ends` (JUST (Date 1 3 2020)) (JUST (Date 1 3 2019)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2020)   -- the same day
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(4) the day on which the obligation under subsection (2) ends` NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 3 2019)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2020)   -- never served: one year after the advice
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(4) the day on which the obligation under subsection (2) ends` (JUST (Date 1 9 2019)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2019)   -- no advice given: the day served
#ASSERT `s 490.02911(4) the day on which the obligation under subsection (2) ends` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
